<!-- to initialise alembic -->

### $alembic init -t async migrations

<!-- which creates migrations folder and files to track version -->

<!-- If you already created a db and table manually and try to replace with alembic you will get
    empty upgrade/downgrade method version file. So drop table and version from local mySQL and run below
    command again. -->

### alembic revision --autogenerate -m "initial_orders_table"

<!-- Now to make sure MYSQL db is completely in sync with our version file, run below command -->

### alembic upgrade head
